\subsection{Scale Validation}

To test whether the item-dominated variance structure is scale-invariant, we conduct a within-family analysis using Qwen2.5 at two parameter scales (3B-Instruct and 7B-Instruct) on MMLU under the same BF16 $\times$ 2-temperature $\times$ 6-prompt $\times$ 6-seed $\times$ 4-ordering design. Using a single model family isolates scale as the sole variable. At both 3B (accuracy 0.682) and 7B (0.742), item difficulty dominates: \texttt{item\_id} accounts for 75.3\% and 73.4\%, respectively, and item-related variance (item + model-conditional interactions) reaches 88.9\% and 90.2\%---exceeding the 8-model cross-MMLU value of 68.1\% because the single-model design eliminates model$\times$item interaction. Generalizability coefficients ($G = 0.963$ and $0.956$) confirm that 200 items yield reliable measurements across scales. [72B PENDING]

